From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:16:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: drop the enforce-E2EE switch and plain-email chat
 cloning

Plaintext email is removed from this build (core/1027 pins
force_encryption on). With it pinned, upstream's own force_encryption
gates already hide "New E-Mail" and adding a contact by bare address;
this removes the two UI paths left over:

- the "Enforce end-to-end encryption" switch in the advanced login
  options, plus the state and setCoreSetting plumbing in
  AccountSetupScreen and EditAccountAndPasswordDialog. Manual login with
  a normal email account stays as it is.
- "Clone Chat" on an unencrypted group, which reopened the plain-email
  draft dialog (subject + address recipients).
